            {
                "entry_id": "5d173a83-c304-3e13-94e7-352328994ce7",
                "word": "bourdon",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "8346d8b4-ff89-4b68-91ac-6d7e9b2801e9",
                        "entry_id": "5d173a83-c304-3e13-94e7-352328994ce7",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "bourdons"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "952620dc-6bcb-36e3-b817-0005a80099b9",
                        "entry_id": "5d173a83-c304-3e13-94e7-352328994ce7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A pilgrim's staff."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "92d7729b-318a-44b7-91e6-088d84a2e0d4",
                                "sense_id": "952620dc-6bcb-36e3-b817-0005a80099b9",
                                "text": "The left hand was gone, this held the bourdon or pilgrim's staff, a small portion only of which appeared over the scrip."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a70fc70a-4421-48e3-ab8f-30702ec8697b",
                                "sense_id": "952620dc-6bcb-36e3-b817-0005a80099b9",
                                "text": "The pilgrim's return was denoted by a bunch of palm, which was tied round the head of the bourdon, the leaves being, of course, ghe guerdon of his enterprise, giving the name of Palmer to the tribe."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "34cff2fe-8b94-496a-acdd-5e5e0591bd7f",
                                "sense_id": "952620dc-6bcb-36e3-b817-0005a80099b9",
                                "text": "Both in Wright's text and in Lydgate's version the hutch from which Grace Dieu gets the scrip and bourdon is said to contain 'many a fair jewel.'"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d5dc765a-2660-4253-9de4-84f82d0e8397",
                                "sense_id": "952620dc-6bcb-36e3-b817-0005a80099b9",
                                "text": "A thin wand is frequently bound against the pilgrim's bourdon in fifteenth century pictures."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
